///
/// \param ini  The INI reader positioned at the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see ProductionUpdateModuleData


/// \class RadarUpdateModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_update_module_factories_c
/// \brief Module data for "RadarUpdate": one radar extend time.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// RadarUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData and shared by every object
/// of the template. Its constructor sets the time to zero. Its
/// \c buildFieldParse registers the class's one table and no base table.
/// Zero Hour: when the radar is extended, RadarUpdate waits this time and
/// then switches the object's model from its extending to its extended
/// condition.
///
/// \par Modding
/// One INI field, read from the retail table: \c RadarExtendTime, a
/// duration parsed by INI::parseDurationReal, exactly as in Zero Hour.
///
/// The instance factory registered for "RadarUpdate" is not documented in
/// this group.
///
/// \see RadarUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *RadarUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "RadarUpdate": builds the module data
///        for one module line and parses its INI block.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration
/// while an `Object` block is read. It constructs RadarUpdateModuleData
/// with its default, then, when \p ini is not null, parses the block with
/// INI::initFromINIMultiProc and RadarUpdateModuleData::buildFieldParse.
///
/// \param ini  The INI reader positioned at the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor default.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see RadarUpdateModuleData


/// \class RadiateFearUpdate
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_update_module_factories_c
/// \brief Update module registered as "RadiateFearUpdate", which also
///        responds to upgrades; configured by emotion pulse settings.
///
/// Its constructor runs UpdateModule's constructor and UpgradeMux's
/// constructor and schedules the module with UpdateModule::setWakeFrame.
/// When the data's \c InitiallyActive is set, it then calls
/// UpgradeMux::giveSelfUpgrade, so the module starts as if one of its
/// upgrade triggers had already been granted. Zero Hour: giveSelfUpgrade
/// plays the upgrade's FX, processes upgrade removals, runs the module's
/// upgrade action and marks the upgrade as executed. The matched BFME 2
/// body makes four virtual calls, the last with the argument 1, which fits
/// the same sequence; the BFME 2 meaning of each call is not confirmed. Its
/// registration adds the bit Zero Hour uses for the upgrade interface, and
/// its data accepts upgrade-trigger fields, so it is an update module and
/// an upgrade module at once. Neither Zero
/// Hour nor Open-BFME-1's \c game/ tree has the class. The field names
/// suggest it sends periodic pulses that cause fear or terror in objects
/// its filter allows; that is an inference from the names, and the
/// module's logic is not described here.
///
/// \see RadiateFearUpdate::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      RadiateFearUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class RadiateFearUpdateModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_update_module_factories_c
/// \brief Module data for RadiateFearUpdate: upgrade triggers plus emotion
///        pulse settings.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// RadiateFearUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData and shared by every
/// object of the template. Its \c buildFieldParse adds two tables: first a
/// shared table of upgrade-trigger fields, placed at an offset inside the
/// data, then its own table.
///
/// \par Modding
/// INI fields, read from the retail tables:
/// - upgrade triggers: \c TriggeredBy, \c ConflictsWith,
///   \c RequiresAllTriggers, \c RequiresAllConflictingTriggers,
///   \c CustomAnimAndDuration and \c Permanent. The upgrades they name are
///   defined in `Upgrade` blocks (\ref page_core_frameworks_upgrades).
/// - own fields: \c InitiallyActive, \c GenerateTerror, \c GenerateFear
///   and \c GenerateUncontrollableFear (booleans), \c WhichSpecialPower (a
///   plain integer), \c EmotionPulseRadius (a real number),
///   \c EmotionPulseInterval (a duration) and \c VictimFilter (an object
///   filter).

/// \fn Module *RadiateFearUpdate::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "RadiateFearUpdate": creates the
///        module for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration when an
/// object whose template lists the module is built. The group page
/// describes the shared pattern.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's RadiateFearUpdateModuleData for this
///                    module line.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see RadiateFearUpdate, RadiateFearUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *RadiateFearUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "RadiateFearUpdate": builds the
///        module data for one module line and parses its INI block.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration
/// while an `Object` block is read. It constructs
/// RadiateFearUpdateModuleData with its defaults, then, when \p ini is not
/// null, parses the block with INI::initFromINIMultiProc and
/// RadiateFearUpdateModuleData::buildFieldParse, so the block accepts the
/// upgrade-trigger fields and the class's own.
///
/// \param ini  The INI reader positioned at the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see RadiateFearUpdate::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      RadiateFearUpdateModuleData


/// \class RainOfFireUpdate
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_update_module_factories_c
/// \brief Update module registered as "RainOfFireUpdate", configured by
///        rain timing, darkness, emitter height and damage-per-second
///        settings.
///
/// Its constructor runs UpdateModule's constructor first, so it is a plain
/// update module. When it has module data it records the current logic
/// frame and starts an internal ramp value at 1 if \c DPSRampupTime is
/// zero and at 0 otherwise. Its data is RainOfFireUpdateModuleData.
/// Open-BFME-1's \c game/ tree has the class;
/// Zero Hour does not. The field names suggest an effect that darkens the
/// scene and rains damage over an area; that is an inference from the
/// names, and the module's logic is not described here.
///
/// \see RainOfFireUpdate::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      RainOfFireUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class RainOfFireUpdateModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_update_module_factories_c
/// \brief Module data for RainOfFireUpdate: rain and darkness timing,
///        emitter height, darkness level, jitter, damage range and an
///        offset.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// RainOfFireUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData and shared by every
/// object of the template. Its \c buildFieldParse registers the class's
/// one table and no base table.
///
/// \par Modding
/// INI fields, read from the retail table, with the defaults its
/// constructor sets:
/// - \c StartRainTime and \c DarknessFadeTime: durations. The defaults,
///   150 and 120, are stored directly and so are already logic frames,
///   while a value written in INI is in milliseconds.
/// - \c RainEmitterHeight (100), \c DarknessLevel (0.25), \c DPSMin (1)
///   and \c DPSMax (1): real numbers read by INI::parsePositiveNonZeroReal,
///   which raises an INI error for zero or a negative value.
/// - \c JitterRadius (a real number, 0), \c DPSRampupTime (a real-valued
///   duration, 0) and \c RainOffset (a pair of coordinates read by
///   INI::parseCoord2D, both 0).

/// \fn Module *RainOfFireUpdate::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "RainOfFireUpdate": creates the
///        module for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration when an
/// object whose template lists the module is built. The group page
/// describes the shared pattern.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's RainOfFireUpdateModuleData for this
///                    module line.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see RainOfFireUpdate, RainOfFireUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData

